1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,729
Twist a bottle cap, and it rises.

2
00:00:02,729 --> 00:00:04,867
Turn a screw, and it sinks in.

3
00:00:05,267 --> 00:00:07,006
Your twist goes round, flat.

4
00:00:07,006 --> 00:00:09,322
But the motion goes straight up or down.

5
00:00:09,772 --> 00:00:12,068
Aarav fixes his cycle with a spanner.

6
00:00:12,068 --> 00:00:13,937
He pushes the handle sideways.

7
00:00:14,287 --> 00:00:16,511
But the bolt does not move sideways.

8
00:00:16,511 --> 00:00:20,644
It goes straight in, at right angles
to the spanner and to his push.

9
00:00:20,644 --> 00:00:21,617
Why that way?

10
00:00:22,117 --> 00:00:24,186
One rule explains it: the cross product.

11
00:00:24,786 --> 00:00:28,939
Multiply two vectors with a
cross, and you get a new vector.

12
00:00:29,289 --> 00:00:32,188
Its size is A times B times sine theta.

13
00:00:32,188 --> 00:00:35,562
Theta is the angle between
them, tail to tail.

14
00:00:35,962 --> 00:00:40,241
Its direction is at right angles to
both A and B, straight out of their

15
00:00:40,241 --> 00:00:41,141
flat plane.

16
00:00:41,497 --> 00:00:42,397
Up or down?

17
00:00:42,356 --> 00:00:43,794
Use the right-hand rule.

18
00:00:43,794 --> 00:00:45,915
Curl your fingers from A towards B.

19
00:00:45,915 --> 00:00:47,992
Your thumb points along A cross B.

20
00:00:48,592 --> 00:00:50,038
To the motion notebook.

21
00:00:50,038 --> 00:00:52,083
A is three units along the floor.

22
00:00:52,083 --> 00:00:54,366
B is two units, lying on top of A.

23
00:00:54,716 --> 00:00:55,839
Theta is zero.

24
00:00:55,839 --> 00:00:57,220
They make no area.

25
00:00:57,220 --> 00:00:58,869
So A cross B is zero.

26
00:00:59,269 --> 00:01:00,195
Now turn B.

27
00:01:00,195 --> 00:01:03,150
At ninety degrees, the
shaded area is biggest.

28
00:01:03,150 --> 00:01:05,775
A cross B is six, pointing straight up.

29
00:01:06,175 --> 00:01:07,075
Keep turning.

30
00:01:07,058 --> 00:01:10,666
At one hundred and eighty degrees,
they lie in one line again.

31
00:01:10,666 --> 00:01:11,566
Zero.

32
00:01:11,551 --> 00:01:14,199
Past one eighty, B is on the other side.

33
00:01:14,199 --> 00:01:16,417
A cross B flips, and points down.

34
00:01:16,817 --> 00:01:19,842
On the graph, A cross
B follows a sine curve.

35
00:01:19,842 --> 00:01:22,565
And its size always
equals the shaded area.

36
00:01:23,065 --> 00:01:23,965
Slow-mo replay.

37
00:01:23,899 --> 00:01:25,255
Freeze at thirty degrees.

38
00:01:25,606 --> 00:01:26,961
The base is three.

39
00:01:26,961 --> 00:01:30,325
The height is two times
sine thirty, which is one.

40
00:01:30,325 --> 00:01:33,504
So the area is three,
and A cross B is three.

41
00:01:33,904 --> 00:01:36,077
Curl your right hand from A to B.

42
00:01:36,077 --> 00:01:37,438
The thumb points up.

43
00:01:38,038 --> 00:01:40,313
Now swap the order: B cross A.

44
00:01:40,313 --> 00:01:42,306
Same direction, or opposite?

45
00:01:42,306 --> 00:01:43,589
Pause and decide.

46
00:01:46,689 --> 00:01:47,589
Opposite!

47
00:01:47,496 --> 00:01:50,838
Curl from B to A, and
the thumb points down.

48
00:01:50,838 --> 00:01:53,364
B cross A equals minus A cross B.

49
00:01:53,964 --> 00:01:56,664
Now the unit vectors, one step at a time.

50
00:01:57,014 --> 00:01:57,914
Step one.

51
00:01:57,866 --> 00:01:59,371
i cross i is zero.

52
00:01:59,371 --> 00:02:03,908
Any vector crossed with itself is
zero, because sine zero is zero.

53
00:02:04,658 --> 00:02:05,558
Step two.

54
00:02:05,543 --> 00:02:06,946
i cross j is k.

55
00:02:06,946 --> 00:02:08,350
j cross k is i.

56
00:02:08,350 --> 00:02:09,753
k cross i is j.

57
00:02:09,753 --> 00:02:13,705
Go round the circle, i,
j, k, and you get plus.

58
00:02:14,455 --> 00:02:15,374
Step three.

59
00:02:15,374 --> 00:02:18,363
Go the other way round, and you get minus.

60
00:02:18,363 --> 00:02:20,022
j cross i is minus k.

61
00:02:20,772 --> 00:02:21,679
Step four.

62
00:02:21,679 --> 00:02:24,834
For any two vectors,
multiply out the parts.

63
00:02:24,834 --> 00:02:27,448
It packs neatly into this determinant.

64
00:02:28,198 --> 00:02:29,238
Remember this.

65
00:02:29,238 --> 00:02:32,359
A cross B is a vector
at right angles to both.

66
00:02:32,359 --> 00:02:34,323
Its size is AB sine theta.

67
00:02:35,023 --> 00:02:37,089
Back to Aarav's spanner, link by link.

68
00:02:37,439 --> 00:02:40,009
r points from the bolt along the handle.

69
00:02:40,009 --> 00:02:42,287
F is his push, across the handle.

70
00:02:42,687 --> 00:02:45,592
Both lie flat, in the
plane of the spanner.

71
00:02:45,592 --> 00:02:49,445
So r cross F must point out
of that plane, along the bolt.

72
00:02:49,845 --> 00:02:53,443
Curl from r to F, and the
thumb points into the wood.

73
00:02:53,443 --> 00:02:54,942
So the bolt goes in.

74
00:02:54,942 --> 00:02:57,390
This r cross F has a name, torque.

75
00:02:57,390 --> 00:02:58,637
We meet it soon.

76
00:02:59,237 --> 00:03:00,246
Side by side.

77
00:03:00,246 --> 00:03:03,608
The dot product gives a
plain number, with cos theta.

78
00:03:03,608 --> 00:03:06,111
It is biggest when the vectors line up.

79
00:03:06,511 --> 00:03:09,478
The cross product gives a
vector, with sine theta.

80
00:03:09,478 --> 00:03:13,040
It is biggest at ninety degrees,
and zero when they line up.

81
00:03:13,640 --> 00:03:14,673
Now you try.

82
00:03:14,673 --> 00:03:17,934
A cross B is zero, but
neither vector is zero.

83
00:03:17,934 --> 00:03:19,841
What angle is between them?

84
00:03:19,841 --> 00:03:21,125
Pause and decide.

85
00:03:24,325 --> 00:03:26,225
Zero, or one eighty degrees!

86
00:03:26,225 --> 00:03:27,707
Sine is zero at both.

87
00:03:27,707 --> 00:03:30,125
The vectors are parallel, or opposite.

88
00:03:30,775 --> 00:03:32,465
Now, one worked example.

89
00:03:32,815 --> 00:03:34,708
A is two i plus three j.

90
00:03:34,708 --> 00:03:36,288
B is four i plus j.

91
00:03:36,288 --> 00:03:39,164
Find A cross B, and the area they make.

92
00:03:39,664 --> 00:03:40,745
Multiply out.

93
00:03:40,745 --> 00:03:45,300
i cross i and j cross j are
zero, so only two terms are left.

94
00:03:46,050 --> 00:03:48,006
Two i cross j is two k.

95
00:03:48,006 --> 00:03:51,283
Three j cross four i is twelve, j cross i.

96
00:03:51,283 --> 00:03:53,110
That is minus twelve k.

97
00:03:53,860 --> 00:03:54,760
Add them.

98
00:03:54,605 --> 00:03:56,351
A cross B is minus ten k.

99
00:03:56,351 --> 00:03:58,360
It points down, into the page.

100
00:03:59,110 --> 00:04:03,030
The area of the parallelogram
is its size, ten square units.

101
00:04:03,680 --> 00:04:05,142
Now, the exam trap.

102
00:04:05,492 --> 00:04:08,181
Many students write i
cross k equals plus j.

103
00:04:08,581 --> 00:04:11,338
But i to k goes against the circle.

104
00:04:11,338 --> 00:04:13,417
So i cross k is minus j.

105
00:04:13,417 --> 00:04:15,551
Only k cross i is plus j.

106
00:04:16,201 --> 00:04:17,309
Where is this asked?

107
00:04:17,309 --> 00:04:20,886
Cross products from parts, areas of
parallelograms and triangles, and parallel

108
00:04:20,886 --> 00:04:21,786
vectors.

109
00:04:22,014 --> 00:04:23,286
Exam level now.

110
00:04:23,286 --> 00:04:25,863
A is two i minus three j plus k.

111
00:04:25,863 --> 00:04:28,721
B is four i plus lambda j plus mu k.

112
00:04:28,721 --> 00:04:30,284
A cross B is zero.

113
00:04:30,284 --> 00:04:31,837
Find lambda and mu.

114
00:04:31,837 --> 00:04:33,163
Pause and solve.

115
00:04:38,563 --> 00:04:39,840
The answer is A.

116
00:04:39,840 --> 00:04:42,394
Lambda is minus six, and mu is two.

117
00:04:42,894 --> 00:04:45,965
A cross B is zero, and neither is zero.

118
00:04:45,965 --> 00:04:47,922
So A and B are parallel.

119
00:04:48,422 --> 00:04:50,448
So B is a number times A.

120
00:04:50,448 --> 00:04:53,614
Four is two times two, so B equals two A.

121
00:04:54,114 --> 00:04:57,354
Lambda is two times
minus three, minus six.

122
00:04:57,354 --> 00:04:59,486
Mu is two times one, two.

123
00:05:00,086 --> 00:05:01,626
Here is your recap.

124
00:05:01,626 --> 00:05:03,209
Screenshot this card.

125
00:05:06,409 --> 00:05:08,347
Can you answer these without help?

126
00:05:08,747 --> 00:05:09,647
One.

127
00:05:09,243 --> 00:05:12,693
Why is the cross product of
two parallel vectors zero?

128
00:05:13,593 --> 00:05:14,493
Two.

129
00:05:13,996 --> 00:05:16,365
How do you find which
way A cross B points?

130
00:05:17,265 --> 00:05:18,165
Three.

131
00:05:17,797 --> 00:05:21,092
Why does B cross A point the
opposite way to A cross B?

132
00:05:21,992 --> 00:05:26,834
Next time: on a merry-go-round, all
the horses turn together, yet the outer

133
00:05:26,834 --> 00:05:28,333
horse travels faster.

134
00:05:28,333 --> 00:05:29,233
How?

135
00:05:28,850 --> 00:05:31,281
Angular velocity and linear velocity.
